from PIL import Image
from pathlib import Path
p=Path('output/scene-review');out=p/'decor-proposal'
frames=[Image.open(f).convert('RGB') for f in sorted(p.glob('animal-motion-[0-9][0-9].png'))]
frames[0].save(out/'valley-ducks.gif',save_all=True,append_images=frames[1:],duration=500,loop=0)
(out/'wildlife-pass.html').write_text('''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Town wildlife</title><style>body{background:#202720;color:#e8ede6;font:16px system-ui;margin:32px;max-width:1200px}img{image-rendering:pixelated;width:min(100%,1152px)}p{line-height:1.6;max-width:900px}a{color:#b4dfa6}</style><h1>Town wildlife</h1><p>Two ducks patrol separate water routes in the lower valley, with frogs on the banks. Three butterflies visit flower patches, two bees stay near the farm, and two mice scurry near the orchard and logging area. Existing swan and fish preserved.</p><h2>River patrols in play mode</h2><p>Actual game captures sampled every half second. Animals pause for different lengths of time and move at slightly different speeds.</p><img src="valley-ducks.gif"><h2>Setup and checks</h2><p>All eleven animals moved and changed animation frames during the runtime check. Full route segments were checked against terrain before placement, and water/land clearance is checked again while moving. Routes can be inspected and edited on the HabitatAnimal components under Hometown / Town Wildlife Habitats. The optional capybara remains deferred.</p><a href="animal-proposal.html">Artwork catalogue</a>''',encoding='utf8')
